WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
In the year 1449, the young Emperor Yingzong of Ming decided to lead a campaign in person against the Oirats.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.200
Full of confidence, the young emperor decided to lead his troops into battle himself.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.880
Wang Zhen, a eunuch in his sixties, urged the emperor from the side to send out the army.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.440
Standing beside the emperor, Wang Zhen kept saying pleasant, flattering things.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.640
When the Ming army marched to Tumu Fortress, it suddenly encountered the Oirat cavalry.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.560
The long column marched into the valley, and dust covered the bright sky.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.320
Dust flew across the battlefield, and the Ming army suffered a major defeat.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.760
Soldiers ran in every direction, banners fell to the ground, and the scene was utter chaos.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.840
The horses in the camp neighed in fright, and people scrambled in panic to find their way.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.680
Yingzong was unfortunately captured — this is the story of the Tumu Crisis.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.600
Yingzong sat in his tent, gazing at the grassland outside, silent.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.080
The news soon reached Beijing, and the whole court was shocked and worried.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.800
The city gates were shut tight; people lit their lamps and waited for news at dawn.
